# GET_STATUS answered with a virtual wire packet appended.
#
# HAND BUILT FROM THE SPECIFICATION, NOT FROM THE CAPTURE. espi_dump.txt has
# no GET_STATUS in it at all, so nothing independent confirms these bytes.
#
# This is the one place the response byte carries more than a response code.
# 88h is R1R0=10b, RSV=00b, code=1000b -- ACCEPT with "a Virtual Wire (channel
# 1) packet is appended" (Table 3 Note 1, p.30; Figure 21, p.36). The appended
# packet sits ahead of the status trailer, so the response phase runs
# response, count, index, data, status, CRC.
#
# Getting the modifier wrong here does not corrupt one label -- it changes how
# many bytes the response phase has, so the CRC lands on the wrong byte and
# the whole transaction misdecodes.
#
# CRC bytes pasted from tools/crc_ref.py (rule R4): FBh over {25}, 73h over
# {88 00 05 88 0F 01}.
CMD 25 FB
TAR
RSP 88 00 05 88 0F 01 73
